# libs/fonts.commit — UI typefaces (M5: the editor shell)
#
# One line per pinned source, `<kind> <version> <url>`:
#
#   kind    `release`  a GitHub release asset (.zip, unpacked with python3's
#                     zipfile, which is already a bootstrap dependency for ninja)
#   kind    `files`    a list of `path-in-archive destination-name` pairs
#
# Both fonts are SIL Open Font License 1.1, which permits redistribution inside
# a proprietary product — see DEPENDENCIES.md. Nothing here is committed: the
# archives are downloaded into libs/fonts/ and the .ttf files are unpacked from
# them, exactly like Dawn into libs/dawn/install.
#
# Only the weights the editor actually renders are kept. Inter ships 18 static
# weights and JetBrains Mono another 15; keeping all of them would triple the
# editor's font atlas for glyphs nothing draws.

release 4.1 https://github.com/rsms/inter/releases/download/v4.1/Inter-4.1.zip
files extras/ttf/Inter-Regular.ttf        Inter-Regular.ttf
files extras/ttf/Inter-Medium.ttf         Inter-Medium.ttf
files extras/ttf/Inter-SemiBold.ttf       Inter-SemiBold.ttf
files extras/ttf/Inter-Bold.ttf           Inter-Bold.ttf

release 2.304 https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono/releases/download/v2.304/JetBrainsMono-2.304.zip
files fonts/ttf/JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf   JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf
files fonts/ttf/JetBrainsMono-Medium.ttf    JetBrainsMono-Medium.ttf
files fonts/ttf/JetBrainsMono-Bold.ttf      JetBrainsMono-Bold.ttf
